  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Down the board and a hard diagonal ball",
  "description": "Group A stands in the middle of the half with the balls, group B by the right board. A cone is placed a little outside the penalty area.\n\nA passes to B, who takes it at speed and carries on along the board towards the corner flag. Meanwhile A skates round the cone and heads for goal. Near the corner B plays a hard diagonal pass back into the rink and A finishes – first-time shot, drag or deflection. Rotation: A goes to B and B to A.\n\nSwitch sides after a while so the cross comes from both wings. Variant: add a defender who follows A. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Full speed along the board – the first touch must not slow B down."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A times the run and heads for goal as B nears the corner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The cross should be hard and angled back in front of goal, not at the goalkeeper."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish first time – there is no time to bring the ball down."
    }
  ],
